  ~203 candidates on the FULL S&P100 (~105 tickers) with the archive
  growing to ~57 — both the candidate count and the per-candidate
  matrix were far larger than this reduced-ticker diagnostic.
  Levers the numbers above will price out: fewer CPCV folds, a linear
  --marginal-model, parallel folds, freezing the book within a gen.

